# Conventional Commits — write your message on the FIRST line, then delete this block
# Format: <type>(<scope>): <short subject in English>
#
# Example:
#   feat(handlers): add /status command
#
# Types:
#   feat fix docs style refactor perf test build ci chore revert
#
# Rules:
#   - subject in imperative mood, lowercase, no trailing period, <= 72 chars
#   - body (optional): explain what & why, wrap at 100 chars
#   - footer (optional): "BREAKING CHANGE: <desc>" or "Closes: #123"
# Lines starting with '#' are ignored by git.
